{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513592-infernals-abyssals-allow-redemption-or-instead-not-be-related-to-solars","id":1513592,"title":"Infernals/Abyssals: Allow \"Redemption\" or instead not be related to Solars?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-01T18:59:37-07:00","id":1513592,"title":"Infernals/Abyssals: Allow \"Redemption\" or instead not be related to Solars?","content":"I remember in 2E that there was some serious dislike shall we say to the idea that Abyssals could be turned back into Solars.<br /> <br /> Redemption was a dirty word apparently.<br /> <br /> Personally I found that funny as one of the first things about Abyssals that I remember was the Monstrance of Celestial Portion which basically converted Solars to Abyssals.<br /> <br /> Same thing with Infernals, they were basically Solar Exalts with Yozi Juice added.<br /> <br /> Apparently Solars -&gt; Infernals or Abyssals was fine but the opposite was not.<br /> <br /> Now my view was always that if you could be converted one way, you could be converted back. If you did not want Abyssals/Infernals to be able to be converted to Solars then Solars should never be converted to Infernals / Abyssals.<br /> <br /> ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> So my question:<br /> <br /> Would you rather Abyssals/Infernals be :-<br /> <br /> &quot;Converted&quot; Solars but have the option of being converted back to actual Solars (Note: Solars could be converted to Infernals/Abyssals in this scenario).<br /> <br /> OR<br /> <br /> Be actual Exalted of the Never-Born / Yozi's. They were never Solars in the first place.<br /> <br /> In other words 300 Solars wondering creation currently but who knows how many Infernals/Abyssals exist....<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT: Keep in mind that I am not necessarily saying the individual exalt has to go on a 'redemption' arc but that the Exaltation <u>SHARD</u> can be converted back and forth. (The Exalt surviving the process or even wanting or being happy about it? That's an optional extra). </b><br /> <br /> ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Side Note :-<br /> Reason for my question is that I am working on my own setting/background/lore changes and got to the Abyssals and began wondering about this question.<br /> <br /> This is pure setting/background fluff right now as we don't have mechanics for Abyssals/Infernals but I was interested in what people thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4678,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4678-tryingtobeslim","user":"TryingToBeSlim","date":". 06-05-2023, 03:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4678-tryingtobeslim","name":"TryingToBeSlim","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T19:13:02-07:00","id":1513596,"title":"","content":"I'm fine with Abyssals and Infernals being able to become Solars again. Thematically, it fits: the sun rises after a period of darkness; and it seems unreasonable to me that a Solar-level Exaltation should be capable of the kind of legendary impossibilities generally attributed to them but not be able to overcome external corruption inflicted on them. I know it's White Wolf, but the idea that you can only fall and never rise again feels off to me.<br /> <br /> So I'd rather they be corrupted Solar Exaltations than original creations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T20:24:02-07:00","id":1513601,"title":"","content":"Note: Abyssals have always had the potential to become Solar Exalted again, although it was very much framed as &quot;This can happen but it hasn't yet, you'll probably be the first, and this is a big enough deal to be the end of a chronicle.&quot; sort of thing. Infernals haven't been, although IIRC the motivation there was a Watsonian &quot;The Infernal Exaltation isn't an alteration to the core functions of the Solar one, it's a Solar Exaltation encased in an entirely separate thing and powering the Yozi OS.&quot; and a Doylist &quot;The Infernals haven't done things fundamentally wrong like the Abyssal did when they accepted their own Exaltation, and so &quot;redemption&quot; doesn't fit into their narrative.&quot; Likewise, Solar Exalted couldn't be converted to Infernals, at least not the Green Sun Princes; becoming akuma was different, but as far as I care making that decision is a Game Over and you don't get to be redeemed because that means you've completely surrendered narrative agency.<br /> <br /> Now, I haven't looked at Essence, for the most part it's not a product I'm interested in, so I don't know if the current creative team has voiced their plans on how the Exaltations work this time around. For all I know the narrative on the Abyssals has changed significantly.<br /> <br /> Anyway, this is a tricky subject because some folks, such as a former player of mine, will absolutely look at altered Solar Exaltations as a problem that absolutely needs to be solved: Abyssal and Infernal Exaltations alike not only need to be able to be restored to their original natures, but a necessary part of the win condition of the game is fixing them, making them the Solar Exalted they should have been all along. <br /> <br /> I disagree, FWIW--declaring that the only non-asshole way to be a splat is to pursue no longer being that thing is not a conceit I'm here for--but I can at least understand the perspective.<br /> <br /> I don't think I'm directly engaging with your question, though. <br /> <br /> If I were forced to decide, then I would probably cleave the Abyssals and the Infernals from the Solar Exalted. I don't think it's a good idea: if nothing else it severs both of those splats from some of their current hooks, and runs the risk of making Exaltation a little less impressive. However, if the alternative is a focus on the mutability of the Solar Exaltation then it may be a decision that needs to be made. It does them no favors for someone to look at every Deathknight and see primarily a Solar Exaltation that needs fixed.<br /> <br /> This may not be doing justice to the debate, but it's a little late, I'm tired, and I've kicked this question around myself before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T20:47:33-07:00","id":1513602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513592-infernals-abyssals-allow-redemption-or-instead-not-be-related-to-solars?p=1513601#post1513601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would probably cleave the Abyssals and the Infernals from the Solar Exalted. I don't think it's a good idea: if nothing else it severs both of those splats from some of their current hooks, and runs the risk of making Exaltation a little less impressive. However, if the alternative is a focus on the mutability of the Solar Exaltation then it may be a decision that needs to be made. It does them no favors for someone to look at every Deathknight and see primarily a Solar Exaltation that needs fixed.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a good point. From a player standpoint, I think Abyssals as former Solars only work when players aren't aware of that fact and discover through repeated, horrific exposure that Abyssals seems to be perverse desecrations of the (currently and mostly) heroic Solars. Like, yeah, in-game that's still a secret and people are only slowly discovering it as people with experience of Solars survive Abyssals for long enough to make the observations, but the players have known it for decades, so the revelation falls pretty flat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T21:15:29-07:00","id":1513604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513592-infernals-abyssals-allow-redemption-or-instead-not-be-related-to-solars?p=1513601#post1513601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note: Abyssals have always had the potential to become Solar Exalted again, although it was very much framed as &quot;This can happen but it hasn't yet, you'll probably be the first, and this is a big enough deal to be the end of a chronicle.&quot; sort of thing. Infernals haven't been, although IIRC the motivation there was a Watsonian &quot;The Infernal Exaltation isn't an alteration to the core functions of the Solar one, it's a Solar Exaltation encased in an entirely separate thing and powering the Yozi OS.&quot; and a Doylist &quot;The Infernals haven't done things fundamentally wrong like the Abyssal did when they accepted their own Exaltation, and so &quot;redemption&quot; doesn't fit into their narrative.&quot; Likewise, Solar Exalted couldn't be converted to Infernals, at least not the Green Sun Princes; becoming akuma was different, but as far as I care making that decision is a Game Over and you don't get to be redeemed because that means you've completely surrendered narrative agency.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember that being said about Infernals but my view was always if you could be changed one way, you could be changed back too.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513592-infernals-abyssals-allow-redemption-or-instead-not-be-related-to-solars?p=1513601#post1513601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anyway, this is a tricky subject because some folks, such as a former player of mine, will absolutely look at altered Solar Exaltations as a problem that absolutely needs to be solved: Abyssal and Infernal Exaltations alike not only need to be able to be restored to their original natures, but a necessary part of the win condition of the game is fixing them, making them the Solar Exalted they should have been all along.</div> </div> </div> </div>Going into a bit of my own canon, I would like you to consider the &quot;redemption&quot; being forced. Imagine a Solar Circle spell or Artifact like the Monstrance which would restore the Solar shard/exaltation but restoring it would mean it would leave the dead abyssal. (Abyssal drops dead because no exaltation powering them up anymore).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513592-infernals-abyssals-allow-redemption-or-instead-not-be-related-to-solars?p=1513601#post1513601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree, FWIW--declaring that the only non-asshole way to be a splat is to pursue no longer being that thing is not a conceit I'm here for--but I can at least understand the perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>The one problem I did see with Abyssals was that they were &quot;forced&quot; to be slaves to the Death Lords which meant they had to be assholes.<br /> <br /> I do hope the design team allows them somewhat more lee-way; They should be dammed and chained to the Never-born but should still be able to be Non-Assholes at a PRICE.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513592-infernals-abyssals-allow-redemption-or-instead-not-be-related-to-solars?p=1513601#post1513601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think I'm directly engaging with your question, though.<br /> <br /> If I were forced to decide, then I would probably cleave the Abyssals and the Infernals from the Solar Exalted. I don't think it's a good idea: if nothing else it severs both of those splats from some of their current hooks, and<b> runs the risk of making Exaltation a little less impressive.</b> However, if the alternative is a focus on the mutability of the Solar Exaltation then it may be a decision that needs to be made. It does them no favors for someone to look at every Deathknight and see primarily a Solar Exaltation that needs fixed.<br /> <br /> This may not be doing justice to the debate, but it's a little late, I'm tired, and I've kicked this question around myself before.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind that they would now be exalts of former Primordials. I think they would be somewhat impressive still.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4678-tryingtobeslim","name":"TryingToBeSlim","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T07:12:18-07:00","id":1513643,"title":"","content":"I've never had a problem with the idea that the corrupted Abyssal and Infernal Exaltations could be purified and returned to become Solar Exaltations. Personally I don't find that super interesting because I generally don't find Solars to be super interesting in comparison to other Exalted types, but I think the concept absolutely fits into the setting and can make for a cool arc for players to play through at the table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T12:53:27-07:00","id":1513689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513592-infernals-abyssals-allow-redemption-or-instead-not-be-related-to-solars?p=1513643#post1513643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never had a problem with the idea that the corrupted Abyssal and Infernal Exaltations could be purified and returned to become Solar Exaltations. Personally I don't find that super interesting because I generally don't find Solars to be super interesting in comparison to other Exalted types, but I think the concept absolutely fits into the setting and can make for a cool arc for players to play through at the table.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm mostly in the same camp - yes, the redemption/purification is a possible story arc, <b>if</b> the connection is known/made IC and of interest to the player and ST.<br /> <br /> But to be 100% honest, most of time <i><b>hasn't</b></i> been, because all of the Green Sun Princes i've seen in the table were more interested on either ganking/usurping the Yozis or transcending into Devil-Tigers, when not both and the Deathknights perfectly fine with playing with the &quot;dark but good&quot; narrative of trying to balance their morals against Ressonance. Most people pick them for the exalts themselves, <b>not</b> for the redemption arc, that will leave them as &quot;just&quot; another vanilla Solar, so to speak.<br /> <br /> That said, it can work very well for a little twist within a 1st Age game, with a Solar that <b><i>by delving into things best left untouched</i></b> finds itself the victim of cronenbergian experiences in becoming a forerunner of sorts to canon Abyssals or Infernals, seeking to purify itself, while minimizing the spread of the &quot;taint&quot; in its debased essence with its alien urges, upon Creation. It can lead to very engrossing roleplay, especially with another &quot;fallen&quot;, far more interested in delving into the mysteries of one's nature (and possibly unwittingly turning oneself in a proto-Deathlord of sorts in the process) as a sort of foil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 04-25-2025, 10:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T13:13:25-07:00","id":1513692,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1147_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1147\" data-vbnamecard=\"1147\">Baaldam</a> &amp; <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar741_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"741\" data-vbnamecard=\"741\">AnubisXy</a> : How would you feel if the &quot;Purification&quot; was Forced? <br /> <br /> For example, Abyssals/Deathlords had the Monstrance of Celestial Portion in 2E. Chuck a Solar in it, get an Abyssal out.<br /> <br /> Infernals/Yozi had let's say stupid process to change Solar - &gt; Infernals.<br /> <br /> If a Solar were to invent the opposite, Toss an Infernal/Abyssal in and get a Solar out kind of artifact.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind this would not necessarily be with the Infernal or Abyssal being willing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4678-tryingtobeslim","name":"TryingToBeSlim","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T13:47:13-07:00","id":1513703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TryingToBeSlim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513592-infernals-abyssals-allow-redemption-or-instead-not-be-related-to-solars?p=1513692#post1513692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1147_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1147\" data-vbnamecard=\"1147\">Baaldam</a> &amp; <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar741_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"741\" data-vbnamecard=\"741\">AnubisXy</a> : How would you feel if the &quot;Purification&quot; was Forced?<br /> <br /> For example, Abyssals/Deathlords had the Monstrance of Celestial Portion in 2E. Chuck a Solar in it, get an Abyssal out.<br /> <br /> Infernals/Yozi had let's say stupid process to change Solar - &gt; Infernals.<br /> <br /> If a Solar were to invent the opposite, Toss an Infernal/Abyssal in and get a Solar out kind of artifact.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind this would not necessarily be with the Infernal or Abyssal being willing.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, doing exactly that hubristic and impractical thing that all too frequently leads to a Deathlord ending with one or more disgruntled, rebelious and outright treacherous lieutenants who will eventually turn on them, causing anything from major setbacks to the doom of the aforementioned Deathlord, except with vectors flipped?<br /> <br /> Well, if the Solar is fine with the fact that by pushing people into that process without really caring to seriously check for individual morals they are simply &quot;painting gold&quot; into what might reveal themselves to be traitorous Deathlord/Neverborn/Oblivion-worshipping bastards or egotistical maniacs that will turn on them big time when they least expect for the sake of their own twisted interests &amp; ambitions, go for it. No reason villains should have a monopoly in hasty boneheaded decision-making. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-05-2023, 07:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T17:33:56-07:00","id":1513728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TryingToBeSlim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513592-infernals-abyssals-allow-redemption-or-instead-not-be-related-to-solars?p=1513604#post1513604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember that being said about Infernals but my view was always if you could be changed one way, you could be changed back too.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> My point on this is that RAW Solars can't be turned into Infernals. It doesn't work that way. Perhaps the Yozis could turn a captive Exaltation between Incarnations into a new Infernal Exaltation, but that's different. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TryingToBeSlim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513592-infernals-abyssals-allow-redemption-or-instead-not-be-related-to-solars?p=1513604#post1513604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going into a bit of my own canon, I would like you to consider the &quot;redemption&quot; being forced. Imagine a Solar Circle spell or Artifact like the Monstrance which would restore the Solar shard/exaltation but restoring it would mean it would leave the dead abyssal. (Abyssal drops dead because no exaltation powering them up anymore).</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> This really was how &quot;redeeming&quot; an Infernal Exaltation worked in the previous portrayal, except you needed no more complex instrument than a melee instrument firmly inserted into the Infernal's cranial cavity, maybe given a couple shakes for good measure, and making sure something's there to catch it and give it to Lytek so he can clean the dross off. You don't even need Lytek or an instrument to stop the Exaltation from fleeing if they're Akuma--again, this is second edition talking and I'm pretty sure this largely no longer exists as a concept--just kill them and their next Exaltation is effectively cleaned.<br /> <br /> Giving that same mechanism to Abyssal Exalted (i.e. we fix you but you die as a part of the process) just...fails to resonate with me at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TryingToBeSlim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513592-infernals-abyssals-allow-redemption-or-instead-not-be-related-to-solars?p=1513604#post1513604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The one problem I did see with Abyssals was that they were &quot;forced&quot; to be slaves to the Death Lords which meant they had to be assholes.<br /> <br /> I do hope the design team allows them somewhat more lee-way; They should be dammed and chained to the Never-born but should still be able to be Non-Assholes at a PRICE.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> FWIW, I actually go a half-step further than you on this. I do feel like it's very specific to the Abyssal narrative--moreso than the Infernal, which also includes conscious agreement to accept the Exaltation--that you have to deal with the consequences of your choice here. It's made under duress, and it's understandable, but you still agree to serve at death's left hand rather than stand in its path. <br /> <br /> I don't feel like you need to be, using your words, damned or chained to the Neverborn in order to be recognizably, serviceably Abyssal. But an Abyssal is, inexorably, yoked to Death, in a sense that maybe no other Exalt has to reckon with. They suffer consequences for denying what they are, but there's leeway in this: maybe they're a killer, maybe they're a champion or a voice for the dead, but they're no more doomed to be Creation's ruin than their Lawgiver counterparts are condemned to mad tyranny.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TryingToBeSlim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513592-infernals-abyssals-allow-redemption-or-instead-not-be-related-to-solars?p=1513604#post1513604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keep in mind that they would now be exalts of former Primordials. I think they would be somewhat impressive still.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> My problem with this happening in either case is it amounts to &quot;who could have foreseen our defeated enemies trying to do the exact same thing we could do?&quot;, and again, without significant re-imagining on the part of the Neverborn, the dead primordials having greater capacity for deliberate and directed action. Which, hey, if you're doing then fine. You're clearly doing some reimagining. But as is, the agents most likely to coherently pursue the project to create new Exaltations of the Underworld are Nephwracks and Deathlords. And I strongly hesitate ascribing either with the metaphysical oomph to pull it off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T20:36:33-07:00","id":1513743,"title":"","content":"I'm ok with Abyssals becoming Solars again, <b>depending on how they changed from 2nd ed to 3rd</b>. It wasn't pushed on them but the idea of the Monstrance of Celestial Portion converting Solars into Abyssals essentially necessitated a narrative counter point in the form of Redemption. Given how Abyssals in 2nd ed were tied to the barely conscious insane and <i>distant</i> Neverborn, only directed by the implicitly weaker Deathlords (if only because an experienced Abyssal could easily take on ghosts/nephwracks one on one). It made sense<br /> 3rd edition has heavily implied that Abyssals will be more heavily tied to the Deathlords, rather than the Neverborn and the former are also implied to be more powerful. But a tighter leash only makes rebellion a more interesting plot hook. A lot of Abyssal play has been about breaking off from the Deathlords &amp; the nihilistic goals of the Neverborn and finding your own way in Creation, a world that rejects the deathly Essence of your being. Redemption makes a lot of sense in that context.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, 3rd edition promised that there is more going on in the Underworld now, so if the new mode of play is down in the domain of the dead and more focused on the knight aspect, I can see the promise of Redemption losing it's shine. If death knights are not intended to being running around topside most of the time in their own stories, then the need to change who they are at the level of their own soul is...less appealing. if the Monstrance does not make a return, then there is less need to &quot;flip the switch&quot; back to light mode. After all, if you can't threan Sloars to go dark, then you don't need to let players have out from said dark.<br /> <br /> Infernals are different. Explicitly, you couldn't redeem them in any of the prior editions. What the Yozis did to their Exaltations was too drastic to undo and furthermore, it could only be done on an unattached exaltation. Additionally, they attracted a different kind of host. Solars were heroes, Abyssals were those who died in the process of their great deeds and Infernals were those who lost. They were the ones who choked, got caught cheating and who, by the their own metric <b>failed</b>. Then along comes the demonic host of the exaltation (and future Unwoven Coadjutor) to make a deal, to give them what can change the fate they have already sealed.<br /> The 3rd edition preview changed this somewhat, along with the Reclamation...but apparently even mentioning that demonic Creators of Creation might get something out of the literal <b>Faustian</b> <b>Bargain</b> they make with their champions resulted in that idea being dropped before the writing on Exalted Essence even began. Even when it essetially boiled down to &quot;Go forth and be Awesome, as it will also make us look Awesome.&quot;<br /> Infernals were never meant be able to undergo Redemption, because they chose to do something irrevocable. Creation itself doesn't reject them, because it knows their makers are the same. They deleted the operating software that Solars &amp; Abyssals run on and replaced it with spirit dna of primordial titans themselves. Instead, them could reach for ascention, becoming living world/titan themselves.<br /> And while 3rd ed Infernals are less &quot;growing souls of demon gods&quot; and do seem to run closer to the original software, I haven't seen any sign that they are intended to play that differently.<br /> <br /> Ultimately it comes down to this: there is play space for unwilling Abyssals right now (though maybe not in their new book) but there is no such thing a someone who exalted as an Infernal against their will. So Abyssals can be &quot;saved&quot; but Infernals chose damnation. Heck there was so much confusion on the matter that most people ignore the first two chapters the Infernal's Manual of Power book because of utterly irredeemable the actions of every Infernal are supposed to be. Absent of new information, which we don't have, Infernals have less of a shot at Redemption than Hearteaters.<br /> <br /> Lillun may be gone, but we don't have anything in the worldbuilding space where she was misused previously. We have that and the rejection of the idea that First Age God-Kings reborn to spread how great the demon god-worlds of Hell are. We don't have enough on 3rd ed Infernals to say if it is possible, only that it was off their old themes.<br /> <br /> So I vote:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Yes, Abyssals should get the option of Redemption</li> <li>No, Infernals don't deserve it and would disservice it if they got it. Hard No</li> </ol>And yeah, I might be a tad salty but how the idea the Reclamation existing as a concept got trashed because...what else did Infernals have that was theirs?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 06-05-2023, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T01:14:11-07:00","id":1513750,"title":"","content":"Mm. This seems to me to be looking at it as a <i>metaphysical</i> thing - the Abyssal and Infernal Exaltations were created from Solar Exaltations, and therefore can be changed back. Making state-changes to the Exaltation.<br /> <br /> A redemption narrative is a <i>moral</i> one - the realisation you've done wrong and making up for it<br /> <br /> Considering the core 3e Infernal narrative is that of the downtrodden and oppressed being bestowed great power, to do with as they will, casting an Infernal-&gt;Solar change as redemption has... unfortunate implications. Is it possible an Infernal might want to change states? Certainly. But it would be a different story from a redemption - a <i>transformation</i>, more.<br /> <br /> For Abyssals, Vance's indicated that redemption in 3e isn't limited to becoming a Solar - it's still on the table, but it's not the only option for an Abyssal who feels they made the wrong decision, or done the wrong thing, and wants to make up for it. Put simply, you can pursue redemption while remaining an Abyssal; it's not necessary to become a Solar, though it's still an option for those interested in pursuing it.<br /> <br /> Plus, it'll be more than possible to be a heroic Abyssal without seeking redemption (we already have an example of that in Adversaries of the Righteous).<br /> <br /> Essentially, the Abyssal playspace is getting broadened beyond the binary of 'kill the world' and 'become a Solar'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-04T03:29:57-07:00","id":1513855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TryingToBeSlim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513592-infernals-abyssals-allow-redemption-or-instead-not-be-related-to-solars?p=1513692#post1513692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1147_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1147\" data-vbnamecard=\"1147\">Baaldam</a> &amp; <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar741_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"741\" data-vbnamecard=\"741\">AnubisXy</a> : How would you feel if the &quot;Purification&quot; was Forced?<br /> <br /> For example, Abyssals/Deathlords had the Monstrance of Celestial Portion in 2E. Chuck a Solar in it, get an Abyssal out.<br /> <br /> Infernals/Yozi had let's say stupid process to change Solar - &gt; Infernals.<br /> <br /> If a Solar were to invent the opposite, Toss an Infernal/Abyssal in and get a Solar out kind of artifact.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind this would not necessarily be with the Infernal or Abyssal being willing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think &quot;Redemption&quot; is a tool better used for characters at the table than something that would be used for NPCs, with the occasional Abyssal or Infernal that the players help through the process. Redemption should be a personal process, that requires an Exalt to spend a lot of time, effort and energy working through, not an automatic or autonomous one. I also think any sort of theoretical reverse process, a process to turn a Solar into an Abyssal or an Infernal should likewise be a personal process and it should require some level of agreement on the part of the Solar in question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-04T03:49:51-07:00","id":1513857,"title":"","content":"As I see it, Infernals and Abyssals are Solar essence modified by &quot;people&quot; not really knowing what they are doing (they're not Autochthon), with a leash added. So, the ST can decide for the game at hand if repairing that is relatively easy, or clearing up the muck-up makes it extremely hard and needs the cooperation of many.<br /> <br /> I don't see redemption to be about repairing that essence to become Solar essence again. Redemption can be about breaking that leash and use their power for good (or even working against their master while still bound to them). Considering Sol didn't have any problem with the Dragon Kings ripping out human hearts and sacrificing them to him, being good have never been a prerequisite to become a Solar. So redemption arcs are also possible for Solars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-04T13:47:23-07:00","id":1513891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TryingToBeSlim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513592-infernals-abyssals-allow-redemption-or-instead-not-be-related-to-solars?p=1513604#post1513604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I remember that being said about Infernals but my view was always if you could be changed one way, you could be changed back too.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I think of it as being like the relationship between vegetables and soup.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-04T22:21:50-07:00","id":1513912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513592-infernals-abyssals-allow-redemption-or-instead-not-be-related-to-solars?p=1513857#post1513857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I see it, Infernals and Abyssals are Solar essence modified by &quot;people&quot; not really knowing what they are doing (they're not Autochthon), with a leash added. So, the ST can decide for the game at hand if repairing that is relatively easy, or clearing up the muck-up makes it extremely hard and needs the cooperation of many.<br /> <br /> I don't see redemption to be about repairing that essence to become Solar essence again. Redemption can be about breaking that leash and use their power for good (or even working against their master while still bound to them). Considering Sol didn't have any problem with the Dragon Kings ripping out human hearts and sacrificing them to him, being good have never been a prerequisite to become a Solar. So redemption arcs are also possible for Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Deathlords/Neverborn didn't know what they were doing. Hence why Abyssal and Solars used to kind of share charms. It was frequently implied that they just reversed polority of the essence and added the leash.<br /> The Yozis were the next most qualified to know what they were doing and the 2nd edition Infernals reflect that; they have an entirely alien charmset compared to other exalts. Nothing structural to the Solar Exaltation remained except the dicecap for charm dice, the ability to learn Solar level Sorcery and their martial arts potential. 2 of the 3 aren't even abilities strictly tied to the exaltation. It was basically a miniature incomplete mismash of Yozi spirit bits powered by/strapped to a Solor Exaltation as stability feature...even then, it was bound in a third circle demon to help keep it together. They were Solars because they kept the ability to act as peers and because they often retained their First Age memories.<br /> <br /> 3rd edition is a different beast and I can't say I've seen enough to definitively say one way or the other but I'd be annoyed if Infernals have a &quot;revert to Solar&quot; Redemption option.<br /> I only use that term, because that is what it was called in MoEP: Abyssals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-05T00:04:55-07:00","id":1513922,"title":"","content":"Slight reminder to everyone: I am happy to see the thread active but I would like to bring the conversation back to the choice I laid out in the OP (Note : I have altered the OP a little.)-<br /> <br /> If you had to choose between:-<br /> <br /> Infernals / Abyssals being altered Solars BUT explicitly able to be converted back to Solars (whether by force or 'redemption' )<br /> <br /> Or<br /> <br /> Infernals / Abyssals being their own separate exaltation. <br /> <br /> Note : I am basically writing/plotting my own Exalted table setting and am genuinely interested in the feedback given those two choices.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4678-tryingtobeslim","name":"TryingToBeSlim","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-05T00:33:33-07:00","id":1513924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TryingToBeSlim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513592-infernals-abyssals-allow-redemption-or-instead-not-be-related-to-solars#post1513592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would you rather Abyssals/Infernals be :-<br /> <br /> &quot;Converted&quot; Solars but have the option of being converted back to actual Solars (Note: Solars could be converted to Infernals/Abyssals in this scenario).<br /> <br /> OR<br /> <br /> Be actual Exalted of the Never-Born / Yozi's. They were never Solars in the first place.<br /> <br /> In other words 300 Solars wondering creation currently but who knows how many Infernals/Abyssals exist....</div> </div> </div> </div>If Abyssals and Infernals having originated among the dead and sealed away Solars absolutely needed to come with the capacity to be turned back, I would take that.<br /> <br /> I think that connection is inextricable for reasons of &quot;I think it harnesses interesting dimensions of the Solar backstory (leaning more deeply into the &quot;they all died&quot; and &quot;they were terrifying tyrants sealed away with a prayer to never return&quot; angles)&quot; and I think it's important for them to all be tied together under the same umbrella of what triggers the beginning of the end of the Second Age.<br /> <br /> Totally separate Abyssals and Infernals means that the return of the Solars becomes important for five minutes before they get swept aside to consider the new hotness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-05T12:08:49-07:00","id":1513961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513592-infernals-abyssals-allow-redemption-or-instead-not-be-related-to-solars?p=1513924#post1513924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that connection is inextricable for reasons of &quot;I think it harnesses interesting dimensions of the Solar backstory (leaning more deeply into the &quot;they all died&quot; and &quot;they were terrifying tyrants sealed away with a prayer to never return&quot; angles)&quot; and I think it's important for them to all be tied together under the same umbrella of what triggers the beginning of the end of the Second Age.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's something there too about how they represent both the legacy of the past (the Divine Revolution, the Usurpation) and the arrival of something new and unexpected. Hope and fear, promise and death and revolution... and reckoning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":51,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","user":"marin","date":". 06-05-2023, 03:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-05T12:23:39-07:00","id":1513962,"title":"","content":"In general, the whole idea of redemption to Solars seem wrong to me, as Solars are not inherently righteous or anything of the sort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-05T12:39:00-07:00","id":1513964,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answer <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a>. Would you mind if I asked for some more details ? Really am interested in your reasoning.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513592-infernals-abyssals-allow-redemption-or-instead-not-be-related-to-solars?p=1513924#post1513924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that connection is inextricable for reasons of <b>&quot;I think it harnesses interesting dimensions of the Solar backstory (leaning more deeply into the &quot;they all died&quot; and &quot;they were terrifying tyrants sealed away with a prayer to never return&quot; angles)&quot;</b> and <u>I think it's important for them to all be tied together under the same umbrella of what triggers the beginning of the end of the Second Age.</u></div> </div> </div> </div>I understand the <u>underlined</u> reasoning, but it's the <b>bolded </b>part that I want to ask you about.<br /> <br /> The problem for me in viewing the Abyssals &amp; Infernals as parts of the Solar Back-Story is that they are so clearly modified from actual Solars. It's like saying you know a Lunar/Side/DB could be a monster if the Yozi/NB managed to alter them. ( I suppose this is why I am open to splitting them. )<br /> <br /> I would view Moray Darktide and Fehim as better examples of the Solars potential of becoming terrifying tyrants etc...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513592-infernals-abyssals-allow-redemption-or-instead-not-be-related-to-solars?p=1513924#post1513924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Totally separate Abyssals and Infernals means that the return of the Solars becomes important for five minutes before they get swept aside to consider the new hotness.</div> </div> </div> </div>In all honesty I think that's already true and happening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4678-tryingtobeslim","name":"TryingToBeSlim","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-05T12:51:07-07:00","id":1513967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TryingToBeSlim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513592-infernals-abyssals-allow-redemption-or-instead-not-be-related-to-solars?p=1513964#post1513964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem for me in viewing the Abyssals &amp; Infernals as parts of the Solar Back-Story is that they are so clearly modified from actual Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know what the future books will say about the nature of that modification. I hope they won't say anything at all.<br /> <br /> In the absence of that (and partially based on propositions by the previous developers), I find myself on a perspective that the transformation of Solars into Abyssal and Infernal Exalted could not have been done in a vacuum. That the circumstances of the Usurpation are a necessary foundational mythology to build upon. The Abyssal Exalted are not merely Champions of Death, they're the great culture heroes who have been slain, passed through the realms of death, and come back changed by the experience and carrying its lessons back to the world of the living. The Infernal Exalted don't merely have demonic powers, they're the monsters of an ancient age sealed away and now unleashed to reclaim what they view as rightfully theirs. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TryingToBeSlim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would view Moray Darktide and Fehim as better examples of the Solars potential of becoming terrifying tyrants etc...</div> </div> </div> </div>Potential is about the future. I am concerned in this instance with the past.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TryingToBeSlim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In all honesty I think that's already true and happening.</div> </div> </div> </div>If so, I will advocate for every inch of ground possible against it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-05T18:12:29-07:00","id":1513982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eltacolibre</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513592-infernals-abyssals-allow-redemption-or-instead-not-be-related-to-solars?p=1513962#post1513962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general, the whole idea of redemption to Solars seem wrong to me, as Solars are not inherently righteous or anything of the sort.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's less about Solars being inherently righteous than Abyssals and Infernals being inherently linked to forces that want to destroy humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T14:31:55-07:00","id":1514049,"title":"","content":"Idea just came to me that I would like to run by everyone, this is sort of me trying to have it both ways for my setting as in keeping a connection but seperating them at the same time.<br /> <br /> What if the Solar Exaltations were unable to actually be converted by both the Neverborn or Yozi's<br /> <br /> BUT<br /> <br /> During the attempt of conversion, they actually created the Infernals / Abyssals based on the Exaltation they were trying to convert.<br /> <br /> ---------<br /> <br /> <u><b>Rough </b></u>Outline goes like this:-<br /> <br /> 1) NB &amp; Yozi's get Solar exaltation shards.<br /> <br /> 2) NB &amp; Yozi begin juicing them up with their magic/essence.<br /> <br /> 3) UCS is connected to Solar Exaltations, UCS notices what's going on and intervenes.<br /> <br /> 4) Both the NB, Yozi &amp; UCS struggle.<br /> <br /> 5) BOOM - The whole conversion process goes BOOM.<br /> <br /> 6) Solar Shards escape and are taken/released by the UCS.<br /> <br /> 7) Yozi and NB find they have somehow created the Infernals &amp; Abyssals by accident.<br /> <br /> 8) Each Abyssal &amp; Infernal is based on a Solar Shard. (Sort of like getting a Clay Mould of a sword and using it to cast a new one) and has memories etc. They can even trigger the Lunar Bond.<br /> <br /> 9) NB are happy. Because creating so many abyssals actually &quot;REDUCED&quot; the NB and made them going into Oblivion that much easier. They NEED to create more so they can enter oblivion.<br /> <br /> 9B) NB are sad. They have found they (because they are dead) cannot create new Abyssals unless they capture an existing Solar (or Infernal) Shard to use as a base.<br /> <br /> 10) Yozi's are terrified. They have been weakened but not actually reduced because they were crafting fewer Infernals AND every single Yozi was giving essence.<br /> <br /> 10B) If there had been more shards or if one Yozi tried to make on their own? They would be reduced. They are not trying to make more. (Note: Yozi's CAN make more by themselves unlike the NB).<br /> <br /> 11) The UCS is upset. The UCS knows that the NB &amp; Yozi have champions equal to his own. The world needs the Solars back.<br /> <br /> 11b) The UCS turns his face back to Creation and while still bound by his word of Exalts being in charge of creation, deciding to do whatever he can to aid behind the scenes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4678,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4678-tryingtobeslim","user":"TryingToBeSlim","date":".  @ Xerxes pointed out that I accidentally cut off part of my post. 06-12-2023, 05:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4678-tryingtobeslim","name":"TryingToBeSlim","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T12:50:39-07:00","id":1514126,"title":"","content":"My main problem here is that by giving the Abyssals and Infernals imprinting from Solar Exaltations they feel even less legitimate. Those memories and the bond aren't their legacy in any real fashion, just xeroxed onto them.<br /> <br /> To the extent they have a Lunar mate, there's still the possibility narratively that their Solar template can waltz in with greater legitimacy, and that makes the Infernal or Abyssal just look bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T14:24:01-07:00","id":1514242,"title":"","content":"I find the tie between Solar and Abyssal/Infernal Exaltations as narratively interesting enough to not want to get rid of it. And i see no issue with having the option to change back. What i just don't want to see is the &quot;Redemption&quot; idea - the idea that taking this path is the only moral choice to take. Being an Abyssal or Infernal should not be a shameful and wrong option you have to &quot;redeem&quot; from. Neither do i want to see this path as the only sensible choice. This one was no issue for 2nd ed infernals (i mean, even if the &quot;turning solar&quot; option existed for them) because in general being Infernal was interesting in itself, and offered other progression paths that were for the most part interesting enough that most players would not want to give them up. In case of Abyssals however it was mostly a non-brained option for any reason except for purely aestethical ones. They were mechanically still Solars, but painted black... and then nerfed some. Anything an Abyssal might want to do, or aspire towards, Solars could do also, and they could do it either better, or the same, but at a lower cost to themselves. There were simply no alternatives to compete with &quot;Redemption&quot; path. I sincerely hope that 3e will change that and offer Abyssals their unique paths and playstyles, in which case turning Solar will just be one of the options, with other, equally or more interesting choices available. <br /> Now, i'm not sure, but from what i remember 3e infernals are actually ditching the Solar link, or am i mistaken?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T22:54:36-07:00","id":1514275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513592-infernals-abyssals-allow-redemption-or-instead-not-be-related-to-solars?p=1514242#post1514242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, i'm not sure, but from what i remember 3e infernals are actually ditching the Solar link, or am i mistaken?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're still the fifty Solar Essences bargained to the Yozis from the Deathlords, and in terms of their capabilities are probably actually making the connection more pronounced.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T02:14:14-07:00","id":1514434,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513592-infernals-abyssals-allow-redemption-or-instead-not-be-related-to-solars?p=1514126#post1514126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My main problem here is that by giving the Abyssals and Infernals imprinting from Solar Exaltations they feel even less legitimate. Those memories and the bond aren't their legacy in any real fashion, just xeroxed onto them.<br /> <br /> To the extent they have a Lunar mate, there's still the possibility narratively that their Solar template can waltz in with greater legitimacy, and that makes the Infernal or Abyssal just look bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>A fair point, I read <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a>'s post and got an idea that I NEEDED to write, should probably have thought things out a bit more.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which:-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513592-infernals-abyssals-allow-redemption-or-instead-not-be-related-to-solars?p=1513967#post1513967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the absence of that (and partially based on propositions by the previous developers), I find myself on a perspective that the transformation of Solars into Abyssal and Infernal Exalted could not have been done in a vacuum. That the circumstances of the Usurpation are <b>a necessary foundational mythology to </b>build upon. The Abyssal Exalted are not merely Champions of Death, <b>they're the great culture heroes who have been slain,</b> passed through the realms of death, and come back changed by the experience and carrying its lessons back to the world of the living. The Infernal Exalted don't merely have demonic powers, <b>they're the monsters of an ancient age sealed away</b> and now unleashed to reclaim what they view as rightfully theirs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you please elaborate on the bolded? Because unless I am missing something, Death Lords might qualify as &quot;the great culture heroes who have been slain&quot; but the Exalt shards have always been separate from the person they attatched too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513592-infernals-abyssals-allow-redemption-or-instead-not-be-related-to-solars?p=1513967#post1513967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If so, I will advocate for every inch of ground possible against it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably a separate thread (You might have seen me post my view at the Sword of Creation), but in all honesty the primary importance Solars have to the current era in 3E (at least from what I have read) is that they are &quot;agents of change&quot;.<br /> <br /> Not that they are Solars.<br /> <br /> Which quite frankly I am upset with because Infernals, Abyssals and even Alchemicals all qualify under as agents of change.Heck 150 Celestial Level Exigents popping up would qualify as agents of change.<br /> <br /> In my view, it's going to be fairly easy for Infernals/Abyssals to sweep away the Solars in terms of importance. Will stop there but that is partly why I want to home-brew my own setting a bit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513592-infernals-abyssals-allow-redemption-or-instead-not-be-related-to-solars?p=1514242#post1514242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find the tie between Solar and Abyssal/Infernal Exaltations as narratively interesting enough to not want to get rid of it. And i see no issue with having the option to change back. What i just don't want to see is the &quot;Redemption&quot; idea - <b>the idea that taking this path is the only moral choice to take. Being an Abyssal or Infernal should not be a shameful and wrong option you have to &quot;redeem&quot; from. Neither do i want to see this path as the only sensible choice.</b> This one was no issue for 2nd ed infernals (i mean, even if the &quot;turning solar&quot; option existed for them) because in general being Infernal was interesting in itself, and offered other progression paths that were for the most part interesting enough that most players would not want to give them up. In case of Abyssals however it was mostly a non-brained option for any reason except for purely aestethical ones. They were mechanically still Solars, but painted black... and then nerfed some. Anything an Abyssal might want to do, or aspire towards, Solars could do also, and they could do it either better, or the same, but at a lower cost to themselves. There were simply no alternatives to compete with &quot;Redemption&quot; path. I sincerely hope that 3e will change that and offer Abyssals their unique paths and playstyles, in which case turning Solar will just be one of the options, with other, equally or more interesting choices available.<br /> Now, i'm not sure, but from what i remember 3e infernals are actually ditching the Solar link, or am i mistaken?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> I agree with most of what you said with a few caveats.<br /> <br /> 1) Abyssals (at least in previous editions) were those who accepted a bargain from the NB or Death Lords. While I might not say being an Abyssal is something shameful and wrong, bargaining with the NB would and should be in my view.<br /> <br /> 2) I agree that &quot;redeeming&quot; into becoming a Solar should NOT be the only moral choice (for either Infernals or Abyssals).<br /> <br /> 3) That being said, it should not be that easy to create/find/follow more moral paths.<br /> <br /> Because otherwise the NB and Yozi's come across as morons. Both factions had a purpose as to why they created their exalts and want to see that purpose fulfilled. Neither are that concerned what the Exalt/Mortal might think/want.<br /> <br /> I am not against Abyssal or Infernals having &quot;moral&quot; options. I just don't want it to come across as if those moral options are the DEFAULT. &quot;Moral&quot; Abyssals / Infernals should be the exception (or PC) and no where near the majority or even a large minority. Problem is with their initial numbers? Even a few examples can become too many. (Note: In all honesty this is partly why I plan on increasing the number of exalts in my setting, 10 Moral Abyssals out of 50 is too many. 10 out a hundred or even two hundred? That's better. Similar things for other splats. )<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4678,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4678-tryingtobeslim","user":"TryingToBeSlim","date":". 06-10-2023, 05:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4678-tryingtobeslim","name":"TryingToBeSlim","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T08:40:41-07:00","id":1514577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TryingToBeSlim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513592-infernals-abyssals-allow-redemption-or-instead-not-be-related-to-solars?p=1513922#post1513922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you had to choose between:-<br /> <br /> Infernals / Abyssals being altered Solars BUT explicitly able to be converted back to Solars (whether by force or 'redemption' )<br /> <br /> Or<br /> <br /> Infernals / Abyssals being their own separate exaltation.<br /> <br /> Note : I am basically writing/plotting my own Exalted table setting and am genuinely interested in the feedback given those two choices.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The comments you make in <a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/viewtopic.php?f=4&amp;t=1245\" target=\"_blank\">your other thread</a> now makes a heap more sense. I think the question you need to ask is what level you want it to make sense on. You were generally given a bunch of thematic answers as to why Solars are relevant, and couched your question in thematic terms (&quot;what makes the Solars unique&quot;, &quot;what's their niche&quot; and so on). What you're actually after seems to be a plot-level answer for why the Solars are relevant.<br /> <br /> For my two-penn'orth, they aren't directly relevant at the plot level because the metaplot doesn't advance beyond their return much. They are released as a consequence of the Yozis and the Neverborn wanting to make Infernals and Abyssals. If you make Infernals and Abyssals their entirely separate thing, there's no reason to break into the Jade Prison, and therefore no reason for the Solar Exaltations to leak out.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a> The thread where TryingtobeSlim is arguing that the Solars aren't relevant to Exalted any more is in the paragraph above, in case you wanted to put some more reasoning into that debate specifically. I also could have sworn there was a version of it in this forum as well (same title and all), but I can't seem to find it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TryingToBeSlim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513592-infernals-abyssals-allow-redemption-or-instead-not-be-related-to-solars?p=1514049#post1514049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>Rough </b></u>Outline goes like this:-<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I really like the reasoning you give for the Neverborn wanting to make &quot;pure&quot; Abyssals, it makes a lot of sense given their main motivation.<br /> <br /> Given that your response was cut off, I'm not sure what else you were going to write, but that set-up as it stands would mean that there's a much more aggressive and co-ordinated Cult of the Illuminated and Gold Faction - with the Unconquered Sun not just back and focused on Creation but with an explicit goal in mind for being so, having the Solars explicitly tasked with hunting down and wiping out or cleansing the corrupted Exaltations would be much more likely. Your setup feels like it forces the idea of redemption (or even just purgation) as a thing that must be done to the Abyssals and Infernals in order to set things right again. Not necessarily that that's the end goal from an Infernal/Abyssal point of view, but it's the right thing to do according to the UCS. I think it actually gives more moral weight (insofar as UCS is the arbiter of morality, so ymmv) to the creation of all three types of Exalted than the current setup.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://wondrousatlas.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">Wondrous Atlas of Creation's Destiny</a> - I cohost an Exalted podcast focusing on examining the setting's lore and how to develop them into elements to use in games.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/924488-homebuilt-exalted-st-screen-reference-sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Ex3 Reference Materials</a> - currently includes an ST screen, common actions sheet, weapons reference sheet, character creation summary and mortal QCs reference sheet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","name":"Xerxes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar497_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T08:40:56-07:00","id":1514578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TryingToBeSlim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513592-infernals-abyssals-allow-redemption-or-instead-not-be-related-to-solars?p=1514434#post1514434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you please elaborate on the bolded? Because unless I am missing something, Death Lords might qualify as &quot;the great culture heroes who have been slain&quot; but the Exalt shards have always been separate from the person they attatched too.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's such a literal way to engage with the subject matter, devoid of its mythic connotations, that I can hardly see the appeal even before the fact that the current trend in the writing is shifting away from it.<br /> <br /> While a Celestial Exalt is not literally the last incarnation of their Essence, nor are they totally detached from the previous member of the chain. There's a link and a lineage which are among the many ways in which the Second Breath entails such a profound sense of transformation that it's given a term that quite directly describes being born again.<br /> <br /> This is something baked into the game's DNA. When Geoff Grabowski, the developer who came up with most of the foundational ideas that made Exalted what it is, described some of the underpinnings of the game, he talked about ideas such as the Founding Fathers of America being born again to lead the nation. The Solars carry ideas such as the mythology referring to how great kings of legend such as Arthur are not dead, merely sleeping until the time of their land's greatest need when they will rise again in glory. That bit at the start of God-King's Shrike talking about beards grown so heavy that they shatter stone tables? That's a reference to genuine folklore, centuries old.<br /> <br /> The Usurpation murdered the Solars of old, and in the Time of Tumult they live again; no modern Solar is totally their predecessor, and how much they are will vary with circumstance and their own wills, but the underlying concept is still there.<br /> <br /> Even if the Abyssals and Infernals don't arise from a literal use of magic to emphasize alternative parts of that backstory to give rise to a different kind of hero, the narrative beats are still liable to inform their presentation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TryingToBeSlim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably a separate thread (You might have seen me post my view at the Sword of Creation), but in all honesty the primary importance Solars have to the current era in 3E (at least from what I have read) is that they are &quot;agents of change&quot;.<br /> <br /> Not that they are Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder which has more significance, being a novelty or having the power to force the Wyld back into the shape of arable farmland.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TryingToBeSlim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which quite frankly I am upset with because Infernals, Abyssals and even Alchemicals all qualify under as agents of change.Heck 150 Celestial Level Exigents popping up would qualify as agents of change.</div> </div> </div> </div>What <i>kind</i> of change?!<br /> <br /> Does nothing seem significant in the distinct Solar powers of artifice, of healing, of swaying hearts and minds, of wrestling gigantic monsters to the ground?<br /> <br /> The Strawmaiden is compelling, but her narrative of being a grand heroic farm girl is far more limited in scope even assuming a Solar who only purchases Charms in the same range as her Strawmaiden Abilities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TryingToBeSlim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my view, it's going to be fairly easy for Infernals/Abyssals to sweep away the Solars in terms of importance.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, that's the other thing. Like, even within the boundaries of thinking that the only relevance any of these things have is in being a novelty, the Abyssals are hardly new. Being a harbinger of death just means helping the world stay the course on its downward spiral into ruin. The return of the Solars constitutes a last ditch effort to reverse that, to revive a vitality in a world whose divisions have brought it to the brink of ruin.<br /> <br /> Infernals I view as intended by their patrons to be somewhere between hastening the end and clawing the world back from the brink and making it beg for an end which will never come. The personalities of individual Infernals might vary effectively within that, but there can be a question of how much range they can express through the nature of their power.<br /> \u200b<br /> And sure, the future of Creation is not merely a competition between the three philosophies of Solars, Lunars and Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded have their say as well. But those Exalted who have been present throughout the Second Age have all lived to some extent under the shadow of the Usurpation, and the return of Solars and Abyssals and Infernals is not merely something to shake up the status quo but a mythos of the Usurpation coming back to haunt them.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T12:07:07-07:00","id":1514598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513592-infernals-abyssals-allow-redemption-or-instead-not-be-related-to-solars?p=1514578#post1514578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Infernals I view as intended by their patrons to be somewhere between hastening the end and clawing the world back from the brink and making it beg for an end which will never come. The personalities of individual Infernals might vary effectively within that, but there can be a question of how much range they can express through the nature of their power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dev commentary on this one is that the creation of the Infernals has nothing to do with any sort of regard for the end - it's an act of spite on the Yozis' part, ensuring that Creation will never again know stability. (Given that, I suspect the Yozis have little interest in an 'everyone dies' scenario, because then there's no-one left <i>to</i> spite.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T16:44:14-07:00","id":1514638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513592-infernals-abyssals-allow-redemption-or-instead-not-be-related-to-solars?p=1514598#post1514598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dev commentary on this one is that the creation of the Infernals has nothing to do with any sort of regard for the end - it's an act of spite on the Yozis' part, ensuring that Creation will never again know stability. (Given that, I suspect the Yozis have little interest in an 'everyone dies' scenario, because then there's no-one left <i>to</i> spite.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's close enough to suffice for the phrasing that fits the pattern of my description of the narrative trajectory of Creation that the breaking of the Jade Prison throws into doubt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T05:23:44-07:00","id":1515102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TryingToBeSlim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513592-infernals-abyssals-allow-redemption-or-instead-not-be-related-to-solars?p=1514434#post1514434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with most of what you said with a few caveats.<br /> <br /> 1) Abyssals (at least in previous editions) were those who accepted a bargain from the NB or Death Lords. While I might not say being an Abyssal is something shameful and wrong, bargaining with the NB would and should be in my view.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that most would-be Abyssals would likely at the moment of taking the offer, understand nothing more from it than they are offered a chance to live again and accomplish great things... and yes, there will be a price, probably a serious one, but one that might seem very nebulous to them? With the alternative being death? Sure, taking that offer is not exactly a heroic deed in itself, but automatically shameful and wrong and immoral? I'm not so sure about it. Solars can turn into much greater monsters, and yet the only potential source of shame would be their actual actions, not what they <i>are</i>. Unless you are an Immaculate Order believer, of course.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TryingToBeSlim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513592-infernals-abyssals-allow-redemption-or-instead-not-be-related-to-solars?p=1514434#post1514434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) I agree that &quot;redeeming&quot; into becoming a Solar should NOT be the only moral choice (for either Infernals or Abyssals).<br /> <br /> 3) That being said, it should not be that easy to create/find/follow more moral paths.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually true for <i>all</i> exalted. Great power can easily push people into ditching morality for convenience, and the Creation as it stands at this point in time does not promote moral behaviour either. It's hard to be clean in a world that is not. Especially when there's no clear path for you to follow. That's not however what i meant. Creation is (quite intentionally) presented as place without black-and-white morality. Except for Abyssals, it seems, where being one was presented as <i>objectively</i> immoral, with going for Redemption or offing yourself offered as the only right and moral options anyone can take. <i>That</i> is what i was objecting to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TryingToBeSlim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513592-infernals-abyssals-allow-redemption-or-instead-not-be-related-to-solars?p=1514434#post1514434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because otherwise the NB and Yozi's come across as morons. Both factions had a purpose as to why they created their exalts and want to see that purpose fulfilled. Neither are that concerned what the Exalt/Mortal might think/want.</div> </div> </div> </div>NBs are already dead, with only tangential grip on reality. So, expecting them to not have full idea of what they are doing - or lack full control over it - doesn't seem unreasonable to me. Not to mention it's been stated more than once that even the original creators of Exaltations were never in full control over the result - and Neverborn (and Yozi) are not really creators of Abyssal Exaltations. They only modified something that already existed. Also, look at 2e Infernals - it <i>was</i> laughably easy for them to flick a middle finger to Yozis if they only wanted to, with barely any consequences attached to it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TryingToBeSlim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513592-infernals-abyssals-allow-redemption-or-instead-not-be-related-to-solars?p=1514434#post1514434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not against Abyssal or Infernals having &quot;moral&quot; options. I just don't want it to come across as if those moral options are the DEFAULT. &quot;Moral&quot; Abyssals / Infernals should be the exception (or PC) and no where near the majority or even a large minority. Problem is with their initial numbers? Even a few examples can become too many. (Note: In all honesty this is partly why I plan on increasing the number of exalts in my setting, 10 Moral Abyssals out of 50 is too many. 10 out a hundred or even two hundred? That's better. Similar things for other splats. )</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, you completely misunderstood me. I do not want more moral options for Abyssals. I want something exactly opposite - i want the morality to remain a completely personal issue, and not be so massively tied to the splat as a whole. I am okay with seeing an approach &quot;You are an Abyssal, given powers to do Bad Stuff, so you will likely end up doing a lot of Bad Stuff and have an increased chance of ending as a Bad Guy&quot;, but would not want to see &quot;You are Abyssal, so you are Bad and should feel bad about it&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":434,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","user":"Astralporing","date":". 06-15-2023, 08:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T07:40:46-07:00","id":1515125,"title":"","content":"I feel as though Second Edition got to a point where the primary reason to want to become a Solar was because of how Resonance worked. It wasn't that Abyssals had a difficult time doing something other than killing the world because of strictures in their powers or some common inclination in their character, it was that trying to do so would cause them to build up a pressure that would periodically explode through things that the Abyssal probably wouldn't want so cursed.<br /> <br /> Third Edition Abyssals won't have Resonance, and I gather that the Chivalry of Death will have a bit more nuance.<br /> <br /> To say &quot;it should be hard to create a moral path&quot; raises the question of what is immoral in the path that is assumed to be most common to them. Some of those answers should be measured against other Exalted; there are plenty of Dragon-Blooded and Lunar conquerors (and the latter includes many who aren't killing for conquest but are still killing), and Sidereals enforce a system whose decisions on whether or not people die is informed somewhere between obscure esoteric and the self-interest of venal and corrupt gods.<br /> <br /> And some of those answers should be measured against the fact that the dead are people too, and can get something out of having Givers of their own Law to be champions for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T09:21:37-07:00","id":1515139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513592-infernals-abyssals-allow-redemption-or-instead-not-be-related-to-solars?p=1515125#post1515125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereals enforce a system whose decisions on whether or not people die is informed somewhere between obscure esoteric and the self-interest of venal and corrupt gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>All Sidereals are bastards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T11:50:18-07:00","id":1515275,"title":"","content":"I don't know, the only real problem I had with infernals was the whole lilune thing, that was garbage and any time I suggest exalted to someone I give them a quick disclaimer about that whole chapter.<br /> <br /> honestly, I'd be satisfied as long as that gets changed, I liked the whole finding unknown power in the combination of yozi charm trees.<br /> <br /> if I was wish listing it though, I'd want multiple exalt types at each level of exalted power, so Solar and Primordial exalts being on the same level (I saw some homebrew that basically super charged terrestrials that brought their individual power up to that of infernals and abyssals a long time ago and have since lost the homebrew)<br /> <br /> I'll admit I don't know a whole lot about the Abyssals, I loved their setting but they just didn't grab me so I won't talk to much about anything being changed really with them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T00:58:07-07:00","id":1515334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513592-infernals-abyssals-allow-redemption-or-instead-not-be-related-to-solars?p=1515139#post1515139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All Sidereals are bastards.</div> </div> </div> </div>Respectfully, I think the conversation needs to move a bit past the old memes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T05:33:56-07:00","id":1515351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1513592-infernals-abyssals-allow-redemption-or-instead-not-be-related-to-solars?p=1515334#post1515334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Respectfully, I think the conversation needs to move a bit past the old memes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry. Didn't know that was an old meme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T18:54:06-07:00","id":1517022,"title":"","content":"Other people have said it already, but might as well give my 2.5 cents. Yes, I'm fine with them being corrupted Solar shards. Yes, I'm fine with them having the potential to be redeemed. But as a player I find the whole premise of &quot;redemption by turning back into a Solar shard&quot; rather boring and a reductive statement about morality in Creation.<br /> <br /> I'm just saying. You can feed more people with those locust plagues with less effort than you can with any <i>one </i>Solar charm at equivalent Essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26460-organ-boy","name":"Organ Boy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}